{%- comment -%}
  Resolves a named step of a *fluid scale* to its endpoints, and prints them
  comma-separated for the caller to split.

  A fluid scale is not one number. `--fs-display` is a clamp of three — a floor,
  a growth rate and a ceiling — and the theme exposed all three as separate
  sliders, so a merchant wanting larger display headings had to move `display_min`,
  `display_grow` and `display_max` in step and keep them consistent. Nothing
  told them the three were one decision, and two of them out of proportion is
  how a heading ends up clamped to a constant. Thirteen sliders across five
  scales are five steps here.

  Every number below is a proportional departure from the reference design's
  own, which is always `md` — the default, and the only rung the design states.
  That is the rule the whole theme is built to: settings exist so a merchant can
  depart from the design, never so the theme starts somewhere near it.

  **Prints numbers, never keywords or units.** Each of these lands in Liquid
  arithmetic in theme-tokens.liquid — slopes, intercepts and ratio powers — and
  then inside a `clamp()`. A keyword would survive Liquid and produce an invalid
  declaration, which CSS drops entirely rather than falling back.

  Accepts:
    scale - one of: type_base, gutter, space_base, display, section_heading
    step  - xs | sm | md | lg | xl

  Prints:
    type_base, gutter, space_base   "<min>,<max>"
    display, section_heading        "<min>,<grow>,<max>"   grow is per-mille of
                                    viewport width; the caller divides by 10.

  An unrecognised pair prints nothing so the caller's fallback stands.

  Usage:
    {%- capture v -%}{%- render 'scale-step', scale: 'type_base', step: settings.type_base -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign v = v | split: ',' -%}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- case scale -%}

  {%- when 'type_base' -%}
    {%- case step -%}
      {%- when 'xs' -%}12,13
      {%- when 'sm' -%}13,14
      {%- when 'md' -%}15,16
      {%- when 'lg' -%}17,18
      {%- when 'xl' -%}19,21
    {%- endcase -%}

  {%- when 'gutter' -%}
    {%- case step -%}
      {%- when 'xs' -%}10,24
      {%- when 'sm' -%}14,34
      {%- when 'md' -%}18,44
      {%- when 'lg' -%}24,58
      {%- when 'xl' -%}30,74
    {%- endcase -%}

  {%- when 'space_base' -%}
    {%- case step -%}
      {%- when 'xs' -%}8,13
      {%- when 'sm' -%}11,17
      {%- when 'md' -%}14,22
      {%- when 'lg' -%}18,28
      {%- when 'xl' -%}22,35
    {%- endcase -%}

  {%- when 'display' -%}
    {%- case step -%}
      {%- when 'xs' -%}24,54,78
      {%- when 'sm' -%}32,72,104
      {%- when 'md' -%}42,95,138
      {%- when 'lg' -%}54,122,178
      {%- when 'xl' -%}68,154,224
    {%- endcase -%}

  {%- when 'section_heading' -%}
    {%- case step -%}
      {%- when 'xs' -%}20,24,32
      {%- when 'sm' -%}26,31,42
      {%- when 'md' -%}34,40,54
      {%- when 'lg' -%}44,52,70
      {%- when 'xl' -%}56,66,90
    {%- endcase -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Single-value scales below. Same contract: numbers only, `md` is the
    reference design's own figure except where noted, and the caller appends
    the unit. Several of these land in calc() or color-mix(), where a keyword
    would invalidate the declaration outright.
  {%- endcomment -%}

  {%- when 'body_leading' -%}
    {%- case step -%}
      {%- when 'xs' -%}145
      {%- when 'sm' -%}165
      {%- when 'md' -%}185
      {%- when 'lg' -%}200
      {%- when 'xl' -%}215
    {%- endcase -%}

  {%- when 'display_leading' -%}
    {%- case step -%}
      {%- when 'xs' -%}85
      {%- when 'sm' -%}90
      {%- when 'md' -%}95
      {%- when 'lg' -%}108
      {%- when 'xl' -%}122
    {%- endcase -%}

  {%- when 'display_tracking' -%}
    {%- case step -%}
      {%- when 'xs' -%}-20
      {%- when 'sm' -%}0
      {%- when 'md' -%}20
      {%- when 'lg' -%}40
      {%- when 'xl' -%}60
    {%- endcase -%}

  {%- when 'heading_leading' -%}
    {%- case step -%}
      {%- when 'xs' -%}95
      {%- when 'sm' -%}101
      {%- when 'md' -%}108
      {%- when 'lg' -%}122
      {%- when 'xl' -%}138
    {%- endcase -%}

  {%- when 'heading_tracking' -%}
    {%- case step -%}
      {%- when 'xs' -%}-30
      {%- when 'sm' -%}-15
      {%- when 'md' -%}0
      {%- when 'lg' -%}25
      {%- when 'xl' -%}60
    {%- endcase -%}

  {%- when 'micro' -%}
    {%- comment -%} size,tracking — one decision about the micro label {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- case step -%}
      {%- when 'xs' -%}10,140
      {%- when 'sm' -%}11,180
      {%- when 'md' -%}12,220
      {%- when 'lg' -%}13,265
      {%- when 'xl' -%}15,320
    {%- endcase -%}

  {%- when 'radius_base' -%}
    {%- comment -%} the design is square: `xs` is 0 and is the default {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- case step -%}
      {%- when 'xs' -%}0
      {%- when 'sm' -%}2
      {%- when 'md' -%}4
      {%- when 'lg' -%}8
      {%- when 'xl' -%}16
    {%- endcase -%}

  {%- when 'radius_arch' -%}
    {%- case step -%}
      {%- when 'xs' -%}120
      {%- when 'sm' -%}170
      {%- when 'md' -%}220
      {%- when 'lg' -%}270
      {%- when 'xl' -%}320
    {%- endcase -%}

  {%- when 'border_width' -%}
    {%- comment -%} the design's hairline is 1px: `sm` is the default {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- case step -%}
      {%- when 'xs' -%}0
      {%- when 'sm' -%}1
      {%- when 'md' -%}2
      {%- when 'lg' -%}3
      {%- when 'xl' -%}4
    {%- endcase -%}

  {%- when 'hairline_opacity' -%}
    {%- case step -%}
      {%- when 'xs' -%}6
      {%- when 'sm' -%}10
      {%- when 'md' -%}14
      {%- when 'lg' -%}22
      {%- when 'xl' -%}34
    {%- endcase -%}

  {%- when 'shadow_opacity' -%}
    {%- case step -%}
      {%- when 'xs' -%}25
      {%- when 'sm' -%}40
      {%- when 'md' -%}55
      {%- when 'lg' -%}70
      {%- when 'xl' -%}85
    {%- endcase -%}

  {%- when 'button_size' -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      padding_x,padding_y,label_size — one decision, three settings before.
      A merchant wanting a larger button had to move all three and keep them
      in proportion, and nothing said they were one choice.

      Two rungs are the design's own, stated in its geometry note — "Full
      pill. 18px vertical padding, 34px horizontal" is `md`, and its compact
      button is `sm`. The theme previously shipped 28/16/12, which is neither:
      a little larger than the design's compact and a good deal smaller than
      its default. `md` is now the design's figure, so a button left alone
      matches the reference rather than sitting between its two sizes.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- case step -%}
      {%- when 'xs' -%}20,11,11
      {%- when 'sm' -%}26,13,12
      {%- when 'md' -%}34,18,13
      {%- when 'lg' -%}40,21,14
      {%- when 'xl' -%}48,25,15
    {%- endcase -%}

  {%- when 'button_tracking' -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      `md` is the design's own .15em for a framed button. The link variants
      step up to .16em, which base.css derives rather than storing twice.
      It shipped at 160 and so set every button one notch loose.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- case step -%}
      {%- when 'xs' -%}60
      {%- when 'sm' -%}105
      {%- when 'md' -%}150
      {%- when 'lg' -%}210
      {%- when 'xl' -%}290
    {%- endcase -%}

  {%- when 'button_border_width' -%}
    {%- case step -%}
      {%- when 'xs' -%}0
      {%- when 'sm' -%}1
      {%- when 'md' -%}2
      {%- when 'lg' -%}3
      {%- when 'xl' -%}4
    {%- endcase -%}

  {%- when 'button_radius' -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Named for the shape rather than sized, because a button's corner is a
      look and not a quantity. `pill` is 999px, which the browser caps at half
      the shorter side — safe here because nothing animates a button's radius.
      The nav does animate one and must never use a sentinel: see the note on
      `calc(var(--nav-pill-h) / 2)`.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- case step -%}
      {%- when 'square' -%}0
      {%- when 'soft' -%}4
      {%- when 'rounded' -%}12
      {%- when 'pill' -%}999
    {%- endcase -%}

{%- endcase -%}
